<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: It's okay. It was my mistake. We have been talking it through. I will be messaging her later today.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: What did she say?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: She said she understood that it was a mistake, but she is having second thoughts about meeting me now.  Apparently, she is feeling a little gun shy and I can't blame her. I've been explaining my side of the story and I am going to be explaining it as long as she will listen. I'm so embarrassed. I wish I would stop making mistakes like this.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn10le10ob06re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Peter, misunderstandings happen. I wish they wouldn't, but they do.\nI will have used this site for six months by the time next week rolls around and there were a couple of dates that I wish I had have avoided, but for the most part it's been okay.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:   What a comedy of errors.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Peter. How long have you been talking with this person?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: By tomorrow, I'll have chatted with her for a week.", "time": "35000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn10le10ob06re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: One week. You will have talked to this person for one week!\nI wish you wouldn't get too worked up over this one girl that you've known for a week.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I'm telling you  I have a gut feeling about this one.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh boy. Okay. So you think you are going to be messaging after today?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I hope so.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Then don't give up on her, she sounds like she might come around. That said, there are plenty of other girls out there.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  I wish I would find just one though.", "time": "58000", "id": 3}]}}], "_data": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "A Comedy of Errors", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Second Thoughts", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 10, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Wish + (that) + Would", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use \u201c<span class=\"italic\">I wish ...</span>\u201d to talk about things you do not have or do, or you cannot have or do. </br>You use <span class=\"strong\">wish </span>+<span class=\"strong\"> would</span> +<span class=\"strong\"> infinitive </span>to talk about things you would like to change about a situation or a person. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use wish + would about other people who are doing (or not doing) something that you don't like and that you would like to change. You don't normally use it about yourself or about a situation that nobody can change. </br>Example: </br><span class=\"italic\">I wish you wouldn't get too worked up over this girl. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " I wish you would let me help you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I wish I would stop making mistakes like this.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wish they wouldn't, but they do.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I wish you wouldn't get too worked up over this one girl that you've known for a week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">wish + the Past Perfect</span> when you want to talk about regrets. These are things that you did that you wish you could change, but cannot.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: </br><span class=\"italic\"> I wish I had called earlier.</span></br><span class=\"italic\">I wish I hadn't gone out on that date! </span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Future Perfect and Future Perfect Continuous", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span> tense to talk about an action in the future before another action in the future. This is the past in the future. You use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> to talk about what will be happening at a specific time in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span>, you can sometimes think of the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span> tense like the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense, but instead of your viewpoint being in the present, it is in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span> has two forms:</br> <span class=\"italic\">will have</span> +<span class=\"italic\"> past participle, or</br>  am/is/are + going to have + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Unlike <span class=\"strong\">Simple Future</span> forms, both forms are interchangeable.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will have used</span> this site for six months by this time next week. </span></br> <span class=\"italic\"> You'<span class=\"strong\">re going to have talked </span>to this person for a week</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I will have used this site for six months by the time next week rolls around.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "By tomorrow, I'll have chatted with her for a week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You will have talked to this person for one week!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> can be used with <span class=\"italic\">going to.</span><br> <span class=\"italic\">be going to be + present participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">am going to be explaining</span> it as long as she will listen.</span><br> <span class=\"italic\">So you think you<span class=\"strong\"> are going to be messaging after today?</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to run off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to flee; to go away", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't run off yet, there is still dessert.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when you talk about relationships.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "On second thought", "type": "name"}, {"content": "changing your opinion after reconsideration", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On second thought, I will have a piece of cake.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gun shy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "scared of doing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am a little gun shy about horseback riding after my accident last year.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rolls around", "type": "name"}, {"content": "occurs after a period of time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When my birthday rolls around next month, I want a big party.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "a comedy of errors", "type": "name"}, {"content": "many mistakes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Both teams played very badly. The whole game was a comedy of errors.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be worked up over", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be upset by something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't get so worked up over a silly football game.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le10ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research collocations for the words \u2018online' and \u2018dating.'", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I research the meaning and usage of each word.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I teach the new vocabulary to my group members.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I listen to their new vocabulary and descriptions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I vote on which words are the most useful.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look up the meaning of the word collocation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, find an example of a collocation and share with the class.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In pairs, use a computer to find collocates for the words 'online' and 'dating'. ex) online profile, dating history.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find 5 for each word.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Research each word's meaning and usage.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Split the partners and get into groups of three.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Teach each other your new collocations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the new words and their definitions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Vote on which words are the most useful.", "type": "text"}]}]}